  "title": "Data security – Knowledge Base",
  "text": "Knowledge Base\nDaylio FAQ\nTutorials\nBackup and restore\nPurchases\nIssues\nAbout\nDaylio Family Sharing on iOS\nActivity and Mood Statistics\nData security\nDaylio Premium Features\nAll Docs\nAll Docs\nDaylio FAQ\nPopular Searches\nWordPress\nFooter\nLorem\nHome\nDaylio FAQ\nAbout\nData security\n Updated on January 20, 2025\nDaylio FAQ\nTutorials\nBackup and restore\nPurchases\nIssues\nAbout\nDaylio Family Sharing on iOS\nActivity and Mood Statistics\nData security\nDaylio Premium Features\nData security\nEstimated reading: 1 minute\n 15623 views\n\nYour data is stored only locally on your phone. You can optionally make backups to your private Google Drive space or iCloud.\n\nData stored in the app’s private directories is not accessible by any other apps or processes. You (or anyone else) can’t download the data from the app even if you connect your phone to your computer.\n\nYour backups are transferred to Google Drive or iCloud via secure (encrypted) channels. All data stored on Google Drive is encrypted by Google, data on iCloud is encrypted by Apple.\n\nThe most important thing is that only the Daylio app is able to read your entries. We don’t send your data to our servers, so we don’t have access to your entries. Also, any other third-party app can’t read your data.\n\nFor more information on this, review our Privacy Policy.\n\n Still stuck? How can we help?\n\nWas this page helpful? Yes 32 No 6\n\nShare this Doc\nA-\nA\nA+\n CONTENTS\n\nPowered By EazyDocs\n\n© 2025 All Rights Reserved by Daylio",
